A very-slightly modified version of NetHack version 3.0j patchlevel 10,
precompiled for SunSPARC machines, has been uploaded to the public access
ftp archive on wuarchive.wustl.edu.  The configration is currently setup
to keep bone files in a directory on the machine 131.215.131.148.
Individual games communicate with a server on that machine to store and
retrieve bone files from a common directory.

The package contains a ready-to-run playground for SunSPARC machines and
a sources package that you can use to build the same for other machines. 
You are welcome to contact me to setup bone sharing directories on the
machine 131.215.131.148 for other machine types.

Though this is not a very polished product right now, the mechanisms are
robust and I welcome any comments and suggestions for further refinement.

Currently known side-effects of this version are:

    When you go to a new level, and nethack decide to look for a bone
    file for that level, it can pause for several seconds during which
    file transfer takes place.

    If it doesn't find a bone file, an error message will briefly appear
    on the screen.  This is the side effect of borrowing a generic software
    package for use with nethack.

    If the server process dies or the network went down, the game can be
    stopped for a longer time.  The length of time, as well as location
    of the bone directory, is set in an editable configuration file.

